## Notable Constraints
- Active QML UI has been refactored into a preview-first workspace with reusable components and a tokenized theme layer.
- Camera inventory, capability-driven selection, controller-side preflight, and worker-process supervision now exist in the native UI path.
- USB camera selection now needs a shared FFmpeg-backed inventory source so the UI and worker resolve the same backend-native device identity on Windows test machines.
- Preview transport now runs through a capped worker-to-UI JPEG path with latest-frame-only semantics; further optimization is still possible but the isolation boundary is in place.
- Native worker smoke script: `scripts/smoke_native_app.sh`
- Legacy Python UI remains the strongest reference for worker isolation and preview budget strategy.
- Existing git worktree contains unrelated local changes under `3rdParty/depthai-core`.
